====Metro====
{{Main|Zhol Metro}}

The [[Zhol Metro]], known in [[Qymish language|Qymish]] as Ⰿⰹⰵⱄⱅⰺ ''Miesty'' — short for Ⰴⰰⰶⱀⰵ Ⰿⰹⰵⱄⱅⰺ Ⰳⰵⰾⰹⱄ ''Dazhne Miesty Gelis'', or "frequent urban rail" — is ?th-longest metro system in the world. Opened in {{abbr|2284|1897 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, it has ### stations and ### stops spread across ## lines. The network features a system length of ### km, generally with three or four parallel tracks: two tracks for local trains and one or two for by-passing express trains. Around half the system is elevated while the rest is underground. 

====Commuter rail====
{{Main|KAGiZ}}

The [[KAGiZ]]<!--Krajty Aqant Gelis ish Zhol, literally "regional express rail of Zhol"--> ([[Qymish language|Qymish]]: ⰍⰀⰃⰺⰈ) is Zhol's commuter rail network comprising eight [[wikipedia:goniometer|goniometric]] lines with branches and one [[wikipedia:circle route|loop line]]. 

