===National railways===
Zhol acts as the central hub of the national rail network. It has four major railway stations ([[Zhol Northern Station]], [[Zhol Southern Station]], [[Zhol Eastern Station]], and [[Zhol Western Station]]) and two minor ones ([[Vyshir Station]] and [[Zhol Central Station]]), all — except Central — connected to three networks: high-speed rail lines ([[High-speed rail in Qym|AGR]]), conventional speed trains ([[Rail transport in Qym|TGR]]), and commuter rails ([[KAGiZ]]).

===Air===
Zhol is served primarily by the [[King Bacha XV International Airport]], the ?th-busiest airport in [[Meran]], handling over ### million passengers annually, of whom ##% are international travelers, and #.# million tons of cargo. It is located around 32 km southwest of the city center, in the suburb of [[NAME]]. 

[[Princess Zhivalka International Airport]] is a secondary airport, serving mainly domestic travelers with limited short-haul international flights. 

In {{abbr|2440|2027 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, these two airports recorded traffic of ### million passengers, making them the [[List of busiest city airport systems in Basis by passenger traffic|?th busiest airport system in the world]].

===Waterways===
The [[port of Zhol]] extends south of the city center along the banks of the [[Foldava]]. In {{abbr|2440|2027 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, it handled ## million tons of cargo and ##,### river cruise passengers. In terms of cargo volume, it is the second largest port in Qym and the largest inland port in [[Meran]]. Ocean-going cargo ships can also access the port through the [[Royal Canal]], leading to [[Nagur]] and the [[NAME Ocean]]. Icebreakers ensure access during the winter, when the canals are frozen for approximately NUM months each year. 

